@startuml editor-deployment
title Editor - Despliegue y procesos
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Equipo del disenador" as workstation {
  node "Proceso Electron" as electron {
    component "Main process\nmain.js + ipc/" as main
    component "Preload isolated\npreload.js" as preload
    component "Renderer\nAngular build" as renderer
  }
  folder "Carpeta del editor\nDocumentos/HoneyComb" as project
  folder "Datos de Electron\nhoneycomb-settings.json" as settings
  folder "Instalacion\nschema/, engine/" as install
}

node "Entorno de desarrollo" as dev {
  component "Angular dev server\nng serve :4200" as ng
  component "Node.js / npm" as node
}

node "Runtime distribuido" as runtime {
  component "engine.exe" as exe
}

dev --> electron : abre editor instalado
ng --> renderer : ELECTRON_START_URL
node --> ng : npm run dev
main --> preload
preload --> renderer
renderer --> project : IPC y filesystem
main --> settings : recuerda la carpeta elegida
main --> install : catalogo de eventos
project --> exe : levels y assets
install --> exe : Ejecutar lo lanza

note bottom
Desarrollo: Electron carga Angular desde localhost si esta disponible.
Distribucion: Electron carga dist/ y electron-builder empaqueta la aplicacion.
Primer arranque: si la carpeta del editor por defecto no existe, se crea con
una COPIA de levels/, assets/, characters.json e items.json del repositorio.
El renderer carga los dialogos grandes en archivos aparte (@defer).
end note
@enduml
